# The pack payload is a BUILD artifact (P2-5): `python tools/build_asset_packs.py build-local`
# copies the mt6989 encoder and writes the pair's metadata.json here from the private artefact
# store, every byte checked against the census's own literals on the way in and re-hashed out of
# the directory afterwards. NeuroPilot-compiled bytecode must never enter a repo with a public
# remote, and the root .gitignore's blob walls (*.so, *.dlc, *.context) do not cover .bin — so
# this pattern IS the wall.
#
# (P3a) The wall is the WHOLE packaged tree, src/main/assets/, and nothing in it is re-included.
# AGP's asset-pack plugin zips src/main/assets into the pack whole — no filter, and no DSL to add
# one (AssetPackExtension is packName + dynamicDelivery, nothing else) — so every file under it
# ships in the AAB. The tracked .gitkeep that anchored the payload directory until P3a rode into
# the bundle as a zero-byte asset (the packaging probe of 2026-09-25, sheet §8); it is gone, the
# payload directory exists once build-local has placed the part, and a delivered pack holds
# exactly its payload files.
src/main/assets/
